# Update Loop Hygiene

`Update`, `FixedUpdate`, `LateUpdate`, and per-frame coroutine bodies must be **allocation-free** and cheap. Everything here compounds: 0.1 ms × 20 components × 60 fps is your whole frame.

## Zero allocations per frame

No `new` (reference types), no LINQ, no string building, no capturing lambdas, no boxing inside per-frame methods. See the allocation-discipline rule; it applies doubly here.

## Physics: non-alloc overloads with pre-allocated buffers

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — allocates a hit array every call
RaycastHit[] hits = Physics.RaycastAll(ray, range);
Collider[] overlaps = Physics.OverlapSphere(pos, radius);

// ✅ GOOD — reused buffer
private readonly RaycastHit[] _hitBuffer = new RaycastHit[16];

int count = Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(ray, _hitBuffer, range);
for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
{
    Process(_hitBuffer[i]);
}
```

Same for `OverlapSphereNonAlloc`, `BoxCastNonAlloc`, `Physics2D` buffer overloads.

## Cache coroutine yields

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — new WaitForSeconds allocated every loop iteration
while (true)
{
    yield return new WaitForSeconds(0.5f);
}

// ✅ GOOD — cached
private static readonly WaitForSeconds HalfSecond = new WaitForSeconds(0.5f);

while (true)
{
    yield return HalfSecond;
}
```

`yield return null` for next-frame is free and preferred over `new WaitForEndOfFrame()` unless end-of-frame timing is required.

## Cache string-keyed lookups

- `Animator.SetBool("IsRunning", ...)` hashes the string per call — cache `private static readonly int IsRunning = Animator.StringToHash("IsRunning");`
- Same for `Shader.PropertyToID` on material properties.
- Cache `Camera.main` in `Awake`/`OnEnable` (or a scene ref) — don't call it per frame.

## Prefer disabling over early-out Update

An empty or `if (!active) return;` `Update` still costs a native→managed call per instance. If a component idles for long stretches, set `enabled = false` and re-enable on demand. Delete empty `Update`/`Awake` stubs entirely.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No allocations in `Update`/`FixedUpdate`/`LateUpdate`/coroutine loops
- [ ] Physics queries use NonAlloc/buffer overloads with reused arrays
- [ ] `WaitForSeconds`, animator hashes, shader IDs, `Camera.main` cached
- [ ] Idle components disabled instead of early-out `Update`; no empty Unity message stubs
